1
00:00:00,466 --> 00:00:05,213
Volume with a swipe. The round
button: swipe it, tap it, move it.

2
00:00:06,454 --> 00:00:10,939
Meet the round button. In the Simple
style, a small round button sits

3
00:00:10,979 --> 00:00:14,106
on the edge of your screen,
on top of every app.

4
00:00:14,461 --> 00:00:18,596
Swipe up on it. Each bit you
swipe turns the volume up a step.

5
00:00:18,636 --> 00:00:20,296
The level shows on the button,

6
00:00:20,336 --> 00:00:23,511
and Android’s volume
slider comes up beside it.

7
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:25,805
Swipe down to turn it down.

8
00:00:25,845 --> 00:00:29,410
Swipe the other way and it
steps back down just as quickly.

9
00:00:30,245 --> 00:00:32,105
Tap it for the volume slider.

10
00:00:32,145 --> 00:00:36,734
A tap brings up Android’s own
volume slider, ready to drag.

11
00:00:37,423 --> 00:00:42,133
Hold it to pick it up. Keep your finger
on it until it dims and shows arrows.

12
00:00:42,173 --> 00:00:46,965
The long-press menu opens too,
and steps aside as soon as you move.

13
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:49,916
Drag it anywhere, then let go.

14
00:00:49,956 --> 00:00:52,851
Up or down the edge,
or across to the other side.

15
00:00:52,891 --> 00:00:55,376
Let go and it settles on the nearer edge.

16
00:00:56,392 --> 00:00:58,679
Up next: The Quick slider.
